"You" means the individual or the organisation using the Software. If you use the Software for or on behalf of an
organisation (as an employee, contractor or otherwise), "You" means that organisation.

"Affiliates" means every entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with an organisation.
Employees and turnover are counted for an organisation together with all of its Affiliates.

"Small Organisation" means an organisation (a company, foundation, association, sole trader or any other entity)
that, together with its Affiliates, has fewer than 10 employees (full-time equivalent) AND an annual turnover
(or, for a non-profit, an annual budget) below EUR 1 million, measured over its most recent financial year.

"Public Sector Body" means, regardless of its size: any state, regional or local authority (in the Netherlands
including the central government, ministries, provinces, municipalities and water boards), any body governed by
public law, any independent administrative body (zelfstandig bestuursorgaan), any joint arrangement or association
formed by one or more of these, and any comparable body in any other country. In the European Union this includes
every contracting authority within the meaning of Article 2(1) of Directive 2014/24/EU.

"Large Organisation" means every organisation that is not a Small Organisation.

"Derivative" means any work based on the Software, including modified code, fine-tuned or further trained weights,
quantised, distilled, pruned or converted versions (for example for other runtimes or devices).

"Output" means the transcripts, timestamps and other results the Software produces from your audio.


