  c. any purpose, including commercial use, by a Small Organisation that is not a Public Sector Body;
  d. evaluating the Software for at most 30 days, by any organisation, including a Public Sector Body or a Large
     Organisation, to decide whether to take a commercial licence. Evaluation does not include use in production
     or on real cases.


3. Use that requires a commercial licence

All other use requires a separate written commercial licence from the Licensor. This includes, in particular:

  a. any use by or for a Public Sector Body, other than under section 2b or 2d;
  b. any use by or for a Large Organisation, other than under section 2b or 2d;
  c. using the Software on behalf of, or in a product or service delivered to, a Public Sector Body or a Large
     Organisation (for example as a supplier, integrator, consultant or software vendor), even if You are a Small
     Organisation yourself;
  d. offering the Software or a Derivative to third parties as a hosted or managed speech-to-text service or API,
     whatever the size of the provider.

If a Small Organisation stops meeting the definition, it may continue to use the Software under section 2c for 90
days after the end of the financial year in which it stopped meeting it, after which a commercial licence is
needed.

Contact for commercial licences: murmel@the-ai-factory.com.


